title: Pityriasis Rosea
---

# Pityriasis Rosea

- **Definition** - acute, self-limiting exantham affecting young adults w/ no infective agent
- **Epidemiology:**
  - <u>Incidence</u> - quite common self-limiting condition
  - <u>Demographic</u>:
    - Age - young adults
    - Sex - slight female preponderance
- **Clinical features of pityriasis rosea:**
  - <u>Herald patch</u> - characteristic oval lesion (1-2cm) with central pinkish (salmon-coloured) centre, a darker periphery and a characteristic collarette of scale (collarette of scale refers to peeling scales at the periphery of the rash)
  - <u>Papulosquamous erruptions</u> - occurs 1-2 weeks after herald patches with characteristic 'Christmass tree pattern'
  - <u>Post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation</u> - supervenes after initial episode

  
  ![](img/pityriasis_rosea.png)
- **Variants of pityriasis rosea:**
  - Inverse variant (flexural involvement)
  - Mucosal involvement
- **Mx:**
  - Emollients
  - Mild topical steroids
